@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.450 = private unnamed_addr constant [809 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of the `mako` templates.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AMako templates allow HTML and JavaScript rendering by default, and are\0Ainherently open to XSS attacks. Ensure variables in all templates are\0Aproperly sanitized via the `n`, `h` or `x` flags (depending on context).\0AFor example, to HTML escape the variable `data`, use `${ data |h }`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom mako.template import Template\0A\0ATemplate(\22hello\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom mako.template import Template\0A\0ATemplate(\22hello |h\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Mako documentation](https://www.makotemplates.org/)\0A- [OpenStack security: Cross site scripting XSS](https://security.openstack.org/guidelines/dg_cross-site-scripting-xss.html)\0A- [Common Weakness Enumeration: CWE-80](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/80.html)\0A", align 1
