@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.468 = private unnamed_addr constant [789 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of policies disabling SSH verification in Paramiko.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ABy default, Paramiko checks the identity of the remote host when establishing\0Aan SSH connection. Disabling the verification might lead to the client\0Aconnecting to a malicious host, without the client knowing.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom paramiko import client\0A\0Assh_client = client.SSHClient()\0Assh_client.set_missing_host_key_policy(client.AutoAddPolicy)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom paramiko import client\0A\0Assh_client = client.SSHClient()\0Assh_client.set_missing_host_key_policy(client.RejectPolicy)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Paramiko documentation: set_missing_host_key_policy](https://docs.paramiko.org/en/latest/api/client.html#paramiko.client.SSHClient.set_missing_host_key_policy)\0A", align 1
