@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.492 = private unnamed_addr constant [16 x i8] c"root-logger-call", align 1
@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.493 = private unnamed_addr constant [460 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for usages of the following `logging` top-level functions:\0A`debug`, `info`, `warn`, `warning`, `error`, `critical`, `log`, `exception`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing the root logger causes the messages to have no source information,\0Amaking them less useful for debugging.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogging.info(\22Foobar\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport logging\0A\0Alogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\0Alogger.info(\22Foobar\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
