@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.503 = private unnamed_addr constant [659 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for lambdas that can be replaced with the `list` or `dict` builtins.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AUsing container builtins are more succinct and idiomatic than wrapping\0Athe literal in a lambda.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass Foo:\0A    bar: list[int] = field(default_factory=lambda: [])\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\0A\0A\0A@dataclass\0Aclass Foo:\0A    bar: list[int] = field(default_factory=list)\0A    baz: dict[str, int] = field(default_factory=dict)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `list`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html#func-list)\0A", align 1
