@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.510 = private unnamed_addr constant [628 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `typing.ByteString` or `collections.abc.ByteString`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`ByteString` has been deprecated since Python 3.9 and will be removed in\0APython 3.14. The Python documentation recommends using either\0A`collections.abc.Buffer` (or the `typing_extensions` backport\0Aon Python <3.12) or a union like `bytes | bytearray | memoryview` instead.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom typing import ByteString\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom collections.abc import Buffer\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `ByteString` type](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.ByteString)\0A", align 1
