@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.610 = private unnamed_addr constant [813 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `else` blocks that consist of a single `if` statement.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIf an `else` block contains a single `if` statement, it can be collapsed\0Ainto an `elif`, thus reducing the indentation level.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef check_sign(value: int) -> None:\0A    if value > 0:\0A        print(\22Number is positive.\22)\0A    else:\0A        if value < 0:\0A            print(\22Number is negative.\22)\0A        else:\0A            print(\22Number is zero.\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef check_sign(value: int) -> None:\0A    if value > 0:\0A        print(\22Number is positive.\22)\0A    elif value < 0:\0A        print(\22Number is negative.\22)\0A    else:\0A        print(\22Number is zero.\22)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `if` Statements](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/controlflow.html#if-statements)\0A", align 1
