@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.614 = private unnamed_addr constant [669 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `global` variables that are not assigned a value in the current\0Ascope.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `global` keyword allows an inner scope to modify a variable declared\0Ain the outer scope. If the variable is not modified within the inner scope,\0Athere is no need to use `global`.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0ADEBUG = True\0A\0A\0Adef foo():\0A    global DEBUG\0A    if DEBUG:\0A        print(\22foo() called\22)\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0ADEBUG = True\0A\0A\0Adef foo():\0A    if DEBUG:\0A        print(\22foo() called\22)\0A    ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `global` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-global-statement)\0A", align 1
