@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.634 = private unnamed_addr constant [628 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `functools.lru_cache` that set `maxsize=None`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0ASince Python 3.9, `functools.cache` can be used as a drop-in replacement\0Afor `functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)`. When possible, prefer\0A`functools.cache` as it is more readable and idiomatic.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aimport functools\0A\0A\0A@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)\0Adef foo(): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aimport functools\0A\0A\0A@functools.cache\0Adef foo(): ...\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `target-version`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `@functools.cache`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/functools.html#functools.cache)\0A", align 1
