@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.638 = private unnamed_addr constant [443 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for current-directory lookups using `Path().resolve()`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen looking up the current directory, prefer `Path.cwd()` over\0A`Path().resolve()`, as `Path.cwd()` is more explicit in its intent.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Acwd = Path().resolve()\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Acwd = Path.cwd()\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `Path.cwd`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/pathlib.html#pathlib.Path.cwd)\0A", align 1
