@anon.b08dd5f4f09c4be6245191ddd275a566.642 = private unnamed_addr constant [663 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `metaclass=abc.ABCMeta` to define abstract base classes\0A(ABCs).\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A\0AInstead of `class C(metaclass=abc.ABCMeta): ...`, use `class C(ABC): ...`\0Ato define an abstract base class. Inheriting from the `ABC` wrapper class\0Ais semantically identical to setting `metaclass=abc.ABCMeta`, but more\0Asuccinct.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aclass C(metaclass=ABCMeta):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aclass C(ABC):\0A    pass\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `abc.ABC`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABC)\0A- [Python documentation: `abc.ABCMeta`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABCMeta)\0A", align 1
